    "updated_at": "2017-04-24T13:14:46Z",
    "body": "From discussion in #1198, I believe Firefox is willing to match the new spec (with colSpan limit at 1000 instead of 8190).  @tkent-google said he thinks dropping to the limit of 1000 is doable.  @cdumez said WebKit could try.  So it seems like we have some willingness to match it on the part of three of the browsers.  In contrast, the current spec doesn't match anyone.",
