    "updated_at": "2017-04-27T08:07:24Z",
    "body": "AIUI, https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#rules-for-parsing-integers just says \"interpret the resulting sequence as a base-ten integer\", without specifying any limit for how big an integer can be. So then https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#hardwareLimitations applies.\r\n\r\nIt appears in @ayg's [patch for Gecko](https://reviewboard.mozilla.org/r/134046/diff/1#index_header) it parses to `int32_t` but has different bits to represent overflow, negative, other error... and then branches on those to set the value to default/min/max.",
